ice if they went out in a really nice  way sacrificing themselves for loved  ones and also getting a really happy  ending like she mentioned the happy  ending for cap going back with Peggy  Carter  so that's theory number one going on to  theory number two theory number two  comes from you sir gleaming dust the  theory states that ant-man gets sucked  into a time vortex once he gets out of  the time vortex he goes to the Avengers  headquarters and finds out that he's  actually in the wrong time I agree with  this I definitely think that ant-man is  going to go into a time vortex and come  out in the wrong time once he gets out  and realizes that he's in the wrong time  he goes and finds Hank Pym and Janet Van  Dyne to figure out how to travel through  time vortexes once he figures it out he  goes back to the present time and finds  the remaining Avengers from there using  time travel the Avengers will go back to  the Battle of New York and begin to  change the events of the past and  Captain America will come up with a plan  to get the mine stone from Loki  this theory makes a lot of sense ant-man  is stuck in the quantum realm right now  he obviously has to get out somehow and  it could be through a time vortex after  all they did mention it in the  post-credits scene of ant-man and the  wasp and it makes sense to go back to  the Battle of New York and get the mind  stone from Loki so that's theory number  two now on to theory number three theory  number three comes from a 16 year old  living in India named Dutch and by the  way I'm very sorry if I pronounced  anyone's name wrong Dutch's theory is  very simple and to the point Tony Stark  will have to make a very big sacrifice  similar to the one that he did in the  first Avengers film and he will also  create a suit that lets him wield all of  the Infinity stones I definitely think  that in one way or another the sacrifice  part is true and I also think that Tony  Stark will indeed have to make a suit  that's capable of wielding all of the  Infinity stones  even though Thanos completely destroyed  the Avengers and Avengers infinity war I  still think that people underestimate  just how strong he is you have to be a  being of incredible power to even we'll  just one Infinity stone in fact an  infinity war evany Maus says that nobody  has ever wielded more than one Infinity  stone Thanos was the first person so  it's not like somebody can just throw on  the Infinity Gauntlet and undo the snap  they won't be strong enough to handle it  but if Tony can somehow create a suit  that harnesses and distributes the power  of the Infinity stones perhaps he could  survive the power of the stones and undo  the snap but even if Tony did undo the  snap I still don't think he'd be  powerful enough to survive the power it  takes to perform the snap therefore  sacrificing himself to save the universe  so I do think that Tony is going to have  to make some sort of sacrifice and  Avengers in game and he could possibly  make a suit to wield all of the Infinity  stones  moving on to theory number four theory  number four comes from user infinity  Ewok his theory states that Tony and  nebula lose all hope but Captain Marvel  arrives and leads them to a collapsing  neutron star inside of an einstein-rosen  bridge much like The Devil's anus and  thor ragnarok this will take them only a  short distance from Earth and then  Pepper Potts will come and save them in  her rest  you armored Tony gets back to earth and  meanwhile Steve Natasha  Bruce Thor roadie and rocket are at the  Avengers compound Scott arrives and he  is let in once he finds out about the  snap he tells them that he was stuck  inside of the quantum realm and escaped  through a time vortex from here they  will try to figure out time travel but  during this time Black Widow goes off to  find Hawkeye in Japan she finds him and  he says how his family was lost in the  snap and that he left to talk with  sacred people similar to how Doctor